1	// node:crypto and the global WebCrypto object.
2	//
3	// The reference implements most of node:crypto in JavaScript; this binding reproduces its
4	// observable behaviour on top of the pure-Rust primitives in `crate::crypto`:
5	// * instances keep the reference's own properties (`Hash` has `_reg`, `_chunks`, `_used`, a
6	//   `KeyObject` has `_type`, `_material`, `_asym`, ...) and data passed to `update()` is kept
7	//   by reference until it is consumed, like the reference does;
8	// * plain `function`s are constructible and own a `prototype`, arrows are not;
9	// * async variants compute synchronously and deliver `(err, result)` from one promise-based
10	//   microtask (queueMicrotask semantics);
11	// * error messages, codes and the internal frames in error stacks (`at toBytes`,
12	//   `at resolveHash`, `at codedError`, ...) follow the reference; its interpreter eliminates
13	//   tail calls until a function has run 8 times, which a few helpers emulate.
14	
